WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.013
The Earthworms stood at the entrance to the Willow Creek Cemetery.

2
00:00:05.014 --> 00:00:07.133
It had just stopped raining.

3
00:00:07.134 --> 00:00:11.175
Now the last drops dripped from the tree branches.

4
00:00:11.176 --> 00:00:16.865
Gray fog drifted through the evening air and settled over the graves.

5
00:00:16.866 --> 00:00:22.595
"Ooh," said Luke. "Spooky!"

6
00:00:22.596 --> 00:00:29.698
"Yeah!" said Katie. "Like a scary movie! Waa-haa-haa!"

7
00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:34.192
"Why didn’t we come in the daytime?" asked AJ.

8
00:00:34.193 --> 00:00:41.891
"BECAUSE," said Emily, "in the daytime, we might run into another scavenger team."

9
00:00:41.892 --> 00:00:47.689
"Now if there are no more questions, let’s get busy," said Katie.

10
00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:52.232
"We have to check all the old graves."

11
00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:54.081
Emily looked at AJ.

12
00:00:54.082 --> 00:00:58.746
"Since you can’t read, just sit on this bench and wait."

13
00:00:58.747 --> 00:01:03.512
AJ gulped. "By myself?"

14
00:01:03.513 --> 00:01:06.470
"You’ll be our guard," said Luke.

15
00:01:06.471 --> 00:01:09.707
"Call us if you see anything strange."

16
00:01:09.708 --> 00:01:14.458
"Waa-haa-haa!" said Katie again.

17
00:01:14.459 --> 00:01:19.301
"And here—hold on to the bag," said Emily.

18
00:01:19.302 --> 00:01:26.069
"Wait," said AJ. But the three Earthworms disappeared in the fog.

19
00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:30.011
AJ shivered and sat down on the bench.

20
00:01:30.012 --> 00:01:32.889
He put the scavenger bag on his lap.

21
00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:35.520
He listened for voices.

22
00:01:35.521 --> 00:01:39.977
"Here’s one from 1952." That was Emily.

23
00:01:39.978 --> 00:01:44.581
"Here’s one from 1943." That was Luke.

24
00:01:44.582 --> 00:01:49.262
"1917." That was Katie.

25
00:01:49.263 --> 00:01:52.775
The voices floated further and further away.

26
00:01:52.776 --> 00:01:56.201
Then everything was still.

27
00:01:56.202 --> 00:02:00.451
Near the bench where AJ sat was a block of marble.

28
00:02:00.452 --> 00:02:04.255
AJ tipped his head back and looked up.

29
00:02:04.256 --> 00:02:08.303
A gloomy marble lady stood on top of the block.

30
00:02:08.304 --> 00:02:12.478
She was looking straight down at AJ.

31
00:02:12.479 --> 00:02:16.469
"Mind your own business," said AJ.

32
00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:19.135
He moved to the other end of the bench.

33
00:02:19.136 --> 00:02:20.833
He tapped his toes.

34
00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:23.932
He whistled a few notes.

35
00:02:23.933 --> 00:02:26.436
Then he slowly raised his head.

36
00:02:26.437 --> 00:02:31.218
The marble lady was staring right into his eyes.

37
00:02:31.219 --> 00:02:34.548
AJ shivered and looked away.

38
00:02:34.549 --> 00:02:38.597
"Why did they leave me alone?" he thought.

39
00:02:38.598 --> 00:02:40.868
"I’m an Earthworm too."

40
00:02:40.869 --> 00:02:43.859
Then he heard a voice.

41
00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:50.306
"AJ," it called. "AJ . . ."

42
00:02:50.307 --> 00:02:52.402
"Hello?"

43
00:02:52.403 --> 00:02:57.210
"Aaay-Jaay."

44
00:02:57.211 --> 00:03:00.840
"Who’s there?" he whispered.

45
00:03:00.841 --> 00:03:04.265
"AJ! Over here! Bring the bag!"

46
00:03:04.266 --> 00:03:06.243
AJ jumped to his feet.

47
00:03:06.244 --> 00:03:11.983
"Emily!" he shouted and ran down the pathway into the fog.

48
00:03:11.984 --> 00:03:18.219
He found the Earthworms at the edge of the cemetery near a dark grove of pine trees.

49
00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:21.882
They were gathered around an old gravestone.

50
00:03:21.883 --> 00:03:27.360
"This is it—1859," said Katie.

51
00:03:27.361 --> 00:03:29.745
AJ stared at the stone.

52
00:03:29.746 --> 00:03:32.980
"Now that we’ve found it, what do we do?

53
00:03:32.981 --> 00:03:35.795
Put it in our bag?"

54
00:03:35.796 --> 00:03:38.351
"HA!" said Katie.

55
00:03:38.352 --> 00:03:41.897
"No, silly," said Emily to her brother.

56
00:03:41.898 --> 00:03:44.584
"We make a crayon rubbing."

57
00:03:44.585 --> 00:03:47.212
"We better hurry," said Luke.

58
00:03:47.213 --> 00:03:50.206
"The sun is going down fast."

59
00:03:50.207 --> 00:03:52.257
Katie unrolled the paper.

60
00:03:52.258 --> 00:03:54.996
"Luke and AJ, hold the top."

61
00:03:54.997 --> 00:04:00.198
She held out her hand to Emily. "Crayon, please."

62
00:04:00.199 --> 00:04:05.417
Katie placed the side of the crayon on the paper and began rubbing.

63
00:04:05.418 --> 00:04:08.719
The words on the gravestone began to appear:

64
00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:09.846
EMILY

65
00:04:09.847 --> 00:04:12.211
DEAR WIFE OF

66
00:04:12.212 --> 00:04:14.452
AJ looked over his shoulder.

67
00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:17.676
"Did you hear that?" he whispered.

68
00:04:17.677 --> 00:04:20.038
"There’s something in the trees."

69
00:04:20.039 --> 00:04:22.992
The Earthworms listened.

70
00:04:22.993 --> 00:04:26.482
"I don’t hear anything," said Emily.

71
00:04:26.483 --> 00:04:29.320
"Neither do I," said Katie.

72
00:04:29.321 --> 00:04:31.532
She rubbed some more.

73
00:04:31.533 --> 00:04:32.589
EMILY

74
00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:35.177
DEAR WIFE OF GEORGE WATSON

75
00:04:35.178 --> 00:04:36.329
DIED

76
00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:39.091
APRIL 29,

77
00:04:39.092 --> 00:04:41.954
"Now I hear it!" said Emily.

78
00:04:41.955 --> 00:04:46.073
"Something is moving in there!" Katie looked up.

79
00:04:46.074 --> 00:04:49.244
"It’s laughing!" said Emily.

80
00:04:49.245 --> 00:04:53.328
"No—it’s crying!" said Luke.

81
00:04:53.329 --> 00:04:57.796
"It’s the marble lady!" screamed AJ.

82
00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:01.507
"WHO?" cried the Earthworms.

83
00:05:01.508 --> 00:05:06.732
"Never mind!" cried AJ. "Let’s go, Katie!"

84
00:05:06.733 --> 00:05:11.973
"We have to finish!" said Luke. "We need the year!"

85
00:05:11.974 --> 00:05:16.138
Katie rubbed the crayon for the final time.

86
00:05:16.139 --> 00:05:17.173
EMILY

87
00:05:17.174 --> 00:05:19.410
DEAR WIFE OF GEORGE WATSON

88
00:05:19.411 --> 00:05:20.417
DIED

89
00:05:20.418 --> 00:05:24.570
APRIL 29, 1859

90
00:05:24.571 --> 00:05:29.611
"Got it!" cried Katie. "Let’s get out of here!"

91
00:05:29.612 --> 00:05:34.624
The Earthworms ran, slipping and sliding on the wet grass.

92
00:05:34.625 --> 00:05:37.300
"The bag!" cried AJ.

93
00:05:37.301 --> 00:05:40.826
Emily ran back and grabbed the bag.

94
00:05:40.827 --> 00:05:44.350
"Wait for me!" she screamed.

95
00:05:44.351 --> 00:05:47.677
The Tornadoes jumped out of the pine grove.

96
00:05:47.678 --> 00:05:53.514
They were laughing their heads off.

